      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nVoxtral's processor returns raw waveforms (`audio_arrays`), and `call_hf_processor` casts every float output to the model dtype. With `--dtype bfloat16` the log-mel is computed from bf16 audio. This lets a processor keep named fields out of that cast; Voxtral opts in for `audio_arrays`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `audio_arrays` reaches Voxtral in fp32 under a bf16 model. Before this change it was bf16.\n- The log-mel is computed from full-precision audio, as in transformers and mistral-common.\n- No change for any other model (the default is an empty set).\n\n## Validation\n\nProcessor output dtype, `mistralai/Voxtral-Mini-3B-2507`, `dtype=\"bfloat16\"`, current main:\n\n| | `audio_arrays` dtype |\n|---|---|\n| main | `torch.bfloat16` |\n| this PR | `torch.float32` |\n\nEffect on the mel: `VoxtralEncoderModel.compute_whisper_melspec` on 18 TED-LIUM clips (CPU), bf16 vs fp32 waveform input: max abs diff 0.244 and mean relative L2 8.4e-3 (mel range is about [-1.5, 1.5]).\n\nNew unit test: `tests/multimodal/test_processing.py::test_call_hf_processor_keep_dtype_keys`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Reproduce</summary>\n\n```python\nfrom vllm.config import ModelConfig\nfrom vllm.multimodal import MULTIMODAL_REGISTRY\nfrom vllm.multimodal.processing.context import TimingContext\n\nmc = ModelConfig(\"mistralai/Voxtral-Mini-3B-2507\", tokenizer_mode=\"mistral\", dtype=\"bfloat16\")\nproc = MULTIMODAL_REGISTRY.create_processor(mc)\ninputs = proc.get_dummy_inputs(seq_len=2048, mm_counts={\"audio\": 1}, mm_options={})\nres = proc.apply(inputs, TimingContext(enabled=False))\nprint(res[\"mm_kwargs\"].require_data()[\"audio\"][0].get_data()[\"audio_arrays\"].dtype)\n```\n</details>\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: `InputProcessingContext._postprocess_output` mirrors `BatchFeature.to(dtype)`, which is right for features (`pixel_values`, `input_features`) but not for a raw waveform that the model turns into features itself. Voxtral also casts the mel to the model dtype after computing it, so this only changes the mel's input precision.\n\nDesign: a `keep_dtype_keys` class attribute on `BaseMultiModalProcessor`, passed through `call_hf_processor`. Kept opt-in and per-field to avoid changing other models. Other processors that return raw audio could opt in the same way. I have only validated Voxtral.\n\nNo end-to-end WER number is included. I did not have a GPU run of Voxtral before and after for this PR.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
